abstract: >
  Boundary-Complete Relational Dynamics (BCRD) is a research programme studying
  relational quantum dynamics, recoupling and quantum geometry. The September
  2026 five-rung synthesis establishes, at an explicitly Riemannian,
  coherent-nondegenerate, admissible-large-spin, near-flat, local-branch and
  quadratic scope, a controlled four-dimensional quantum-geometric
  semiclassical sector whose leading metric dynamics are those of linearised
  general relativity. The public repository contains curated publication
  snapshots, reproducibility artifacts, release metadata and frozen provenance;
  it does not present the model as a complete Lorentzian, nonperturbative or
  ultraviolet-finite final theory.
